nights have warmed since 1981. Its days have warmed.","rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 68\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>68\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 70\u00b0F, and the record is 82\u00b0F (1916, 2020). The low of <strong>43\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Gulfport's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Gulfport has set <strong>59 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 75 that chance alone would give, and <strong>111 record highs</strong>, more than the 75 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (49). Gulfport's all-time high is 107\u00b0F, on August 26, 2023.","t_chg":"Gulfport's nights have warmed since 1981. Its days have warmed.","p_chg":"Across 116 complete years: Gulfport's average low shows no clear change: \u22120.04\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.10 to +0.02) that includes zero. Gulfport's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.14\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.07 to +0.20), about +1.8\u00b0F since 1894. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1981, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.56\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.31 to +0.81) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.51\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.24 to +0.77). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; January fell. Highs rose in 6 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Gulfport's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.49 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 64.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 2021 (99.13 in); the driest, 1938 (34.64 in). Gulfport almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.2 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 4 daily record highs, 5 daily record lows"}}